.TH WC 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
wc \- print newline, word, and byte counts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wc
[\fB\-l\fR] [\fB\-w\fR] [\fB\-c\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print newline, word, and byte counts for each FILE (standard input by default), and a total line when more than one FILE is given. Reads in fixed-size chunks rather than loading a whole file into memory, so this stays cheap on multi-gigabyte files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-l
Print only the newline count.
.TP
.B \-w
Print only the word count.
.TP
.B \-c
Print only the byte count.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR (print a usage line and exit) and \fB\-\-version\fR. Commands that take file/path arguments also accept \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options, so a file literally named e.g. \fB\-oddfile\fR can still be referenced.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on a general failure (a listed file could not be processed, etc.), 2 on a usage error (missing or invalid arguments).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
.BR mitos\-utils\-compat (7),
.BR mitos\-utils\-integration (7)
